Ideally bless it all, and put it in piles of unique objects, with no
duplicates.
However, this is generally only worthwhile for really valuable stuff
like amulets, or magical armour.

For most stuff, you want to keep uncursed stuff out of the pile, have
no more than 3 of any one item in the pile.

From Rodneys database, on the IRC channel #nethack, on freenode.
polypile[6]: Items appearing in quantities of 2 or more have a (quantity in 1000) chance of merging into one object.  
polypile[7]: Items also have a probability of "shuddering": 1/3 if a wand or cursed, 1/8 if uncursed, 1/12 if blessed (if in quantities greater than 4, 100%, 1/4, and 1/6, respectively).
This will decrease the quantity of the item randomly, cause any remainder not to be polymorphed, and has a one in (luck + 45) chance of creating a golem.


